    {
     "slug": "north-bend",
     "number": 3,
     "title": "North Bend",
     "text": "Riding from Seattle to North Bend was a treat.  Campuses set in forests.  Bridges hopping from island to island.  Tree lined trails.  Also highways.  I learned a lesson about just letting RideWithGPS curate your journey.  I probably should have trusted my senses better and not just followed it down into a valley and up a near vertical hillside, forcing me to carry my bike.  It spat me out, sweaty and covered in debris at some kind of sterile golf village that looked like it was out of Edward Scissohands.  \n\nAnyway, I made it to North Bend and stayed with a kind family who let me sleep in their treehouse for a couple of nights.  North Bend is where a lot of Twin Peaks was filmed, in particular the scenes in the opening sequence.  Very wholesome vibes, I can see why Agent Cooper fell in love with the place.  It's a land where you can forget about the rest of the world and its accelerating decay.\n\n",
     "cover": "1RhZRv2OjqNfBtX009OUbLZyaygwMo4vv",
